-- title:
--   Lattice stalks of an even isogeny translate
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, let $\iota : W(\mathbb F_{p^2}) \to W(k)$ be a ring homomorphism and write $\bar\iota$ for $\iota$ followed by reduction modulo the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\Phi$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $W(k)/p$, i.e. a $2$-dimensional commutative formal group law with a $W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$-action `act` and an endomorphism `varpi` satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi=[p]$ and $\varpi\circ a = a^\sigma\circ\varpi$; assume $\Phi$ is special for $\bar\iota$ (its Lie algebra splits as the direct sum of the two $\bar\iota$-eigenpieces, each an invertible module) and has height $4$ (the kernel algebra of $[p]$ is finite projective of rank $p^4$). Let $hc_\Phi$ witness that the degree-$0$ and degree-$1$ graded pieces of the Cartier module of $\Phi$ — the subgroups on which $a=\tau(c)$ acts by the homothety $\bar\iota(\tau(c))^{p^n}$ for all $c\in\mathbb F_{p^2}$ — are complementary, so that $\Phi$ determines graded Cartier module data $D_\Phi$ with its $N$-module $N(D_\Phi)=(M\times\Sigma)/\mathrm{nRel}$, and let $r_\Phi : \mathbb Z_p^2 \to N(D_\Phi)$ be an additive map which, for every canonical $L$-map $L$ on $D_\Phi$, maps $\mathbb Z_p^2$ bijectively onto the degree-$0$ $\eta$-piece $\eta(L)\cap N_0$. Let $B$ be a Noetherian commutative $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra in which $p$ is nilpotent, and $\psi : W(k)\to B$ a ring homomorphism. Let $E$ be a ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the image of `act` together with `varpi` into $M_2(\mathbb Q_p)$, and $m$ a natural number such that: $E$ is injective; for each $e$, $p^m E(e)$ has entries in $\mathbb Z_p$; and whenever $p^mE(e)$ is the image of an integral matrix $A$ and $Ne$ is the additive endomorphism of $N(D_\Phi)$ induced on classes $\mathrm{nMk}(x,y)$ by the action of $e$ on the Cartier module in both coordinates, then $p^m\cdot Ne(r_\Phi w)=r_\Phi(Aw)$ for all $w\in\mathbb Z_p^2$. Fix $e$ in that centraliser and $m'$ with the kernel of $e$ of degree $p^{2m'}$, and $g\in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_p)$ with underlying matrix $E(e)$. Let $t,t'$ be rigidified objects over $B$ (a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B$, an integer $n$, and a series over $B/p$), with $t$ admissible for $\psi$ and $t'$ admissible for $\psi$ composed with the $m'$-th power of Witt-vector Frobenius, and assume $t'$ is the $e$-translate of $t$ with shift parameter $0$ and Frobenius exponent $m'$: $t'.X=t.X$ and, for some $c\in\mathbb N$, $[p^{c+t.n}]\circ t'.\rho\circ \mathrm{Frob}^{m'} = [p^{c+t'.n}]\circ t.\rho\circ \bar e$. Let $Q$ and $Q'$ be Drinfeld data over $B$ for the uniformiser $p\in\mathbb Z_p$ and the field $\mathbb Q_p$, with $Q$ a Cartier quadruple for $t$ over $\psi$ and $Q'$ a Cartier quadruple for $t'$ over $\psi\circ\mathrm{Frob}^{m'}$. Finally suppose $m'=2j$ is even and $c\in\mathbb Q_p^\times$ equals $p^{j}$. Then for every $x\in\operatorname{Spec} B$ the lattices of $Q'$ at $x$ are the images under $v\mapsto (c\cdot\mathrm{id})g^{-1}v$ of those of $Q$: $N'_0(x)=c\,g^{-1}N_0(x)$ and $N'_1(x)=c\,g^{-1}N_1(x)$.
--
--   This is the lattice half of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_p)$-equivariance of Drinfeld's classification of special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules: an isogeny $e$ of $\Phi$ of even height $2m'$ with $m'$ even translates the pair of lattices attached to a rigidified object by the scalar multiple $p^{j}g^{-1}$ of the inverse of the matrix $E(e)$. It feeds the case distinction on the parity of $m'$ in [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.IsCartierQuadruple.isTranslateEven_or_isTranslateOdd_of_isTranslate`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.IsCartierQuadruple.isTranslateEven_or_isTranslateOdd_of_isTranslate).
